sal** as the effect's\n1333:### 7.4 Transitive requires and cycles\n1354:## 8. The manifest registry\n1356:### 8.1 The module manifest\n1476:### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n1603:### 8.3 What `yin.vm.module` becomes\n1668:to `{name {:manifest m :address a :derivation d :slice {sym encoded}\n1671:that task's lowered `:bindings` and `:module-stores` instance when\n1677:## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n1758:each restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n1769:entry recorded before an attach restores after it at the same pcs\n1784:## 10. File box\n1803:            (attach-image; offset table and image\n1805:             on the walker; closures carry :store-of)              (M4)\n1810:             keys :yin.k/binding and :yin.k/store-of)              (M4)\n1822:          directed free resolution (7.3), the :store-of consult.\n1833:## 11. Completion criteria\n1872:    7.5.1 the `:yin.k/binding` closure variants and `:yin.k/store-of`\n1895:    each restores on its own.\n1904:    restore identities, and every register the loader would have reset\n1906:    image is a row of the offset table, no restore writes `:segment`\n1907:    from an entry, and `:hash` is never a restore key; a continuation\n1909:    every pc by the receiving offset table; two waiters holding\n1945:## 12. Open decisions\n1991:## 13. Reconciliation record\n1993:### 13.1 Revision r6 (round 5, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2020:| or rewound the code space, and    | offset table, never the           |\n2021:| one parent's lowered bindings     | concatenation `:hash`; restores   |\n2024:|                                   | carry image-relative pcs rebased  |\n2033:|                                   | `:yin.k/store-of` the manifest    |\n2042:### 13.2 Revision r5 (round 4, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2081:### 13.3 Revision r4 (round 3, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2099:| and the named/positional mapping  | image from the offset table or    |\n2127:### 13.4 Revision r3 (round 2, `gpt-6-sol`)\n2186:##