{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1660,1832p;1990,2042p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1660\t  its effect's interpretation, and a token it was not handed it cannot\n  1661\t  use. That discipline belongs to the engine's effect handlers and the\n  1662\t  composition's wiring, and it is the only way a `:pure` or\n  1663\t  `:effectful` declaration becomes enforceable at run time. Until a\n  1664\t  composition wires it, a host module's declaration is trusted, and this\n  1665\t  document says so rather than implying a sandbox it does not provide.\n  1666\t\n  1667\tThe scheduler registry's `:modules` map changes from `{name {sym fn}}`\n  1668\tto `{name {:manifest m :address a :derivation d :slice {sym encoded}\n  1669\t:store encoded}}` -- the portable act-1 encoding, never lowered\n  1670\tvalues (section 7.3, act 4). Each task's own `:modules` entry gains\n  1671\tthat task's lowered `:bindings` and `:module-stores` instance when\n  1672\tits require completes; `resolve-var` reads task state, so no task\n  1673\tresolves through another task's coordinates or store. No shim keeps\n  1674\tthe old entry shape: this is a dev-only repository with no deployed\n  1675\tregistries, and a clean break is the default here.\n  1676\t\n  1677\t## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n  1678\t\n  1679\tFive steps, each landing green on all three hosts before the next. The\n  1680\tpredecessor namespace is renamed, not aliased.\n  1681\t\n  1682\t```mermaid\n  1683\tflowchart TD\n  1684\t  M1[\"M1 rename\\nyin.vm.debruijn-linker -> yin.vm.linker\"]\n  1685\t  M2[\"M2 four format records\\nidentity-directed match, bounded parts\"]\n  1686\t  M3[\"M3 stepped core + link runtime\\nfetch = host policy; DHT behind server\"]\n  1687\t  M4[\"M4 require lowers to the linker\\nmanifests, authority, child install\"]\n  1688\t  M5[\"M5 yin.repl wires the four streams\\nper backend\"]\n  1689\t  M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4 --> M5\n  1690\t```\n  1691\t\n  1692\t**M1. Rename.** Move `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc` to\n  1693\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` with namespace `yin.vm.linker`; move the\n  1694\ttest likewise. Update the five design documents that name the old\n  1695\tnamespace (`yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`,\n  1696\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1697\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1698\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1699\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1700\t\n  1701\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1702\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1703\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1704\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1705\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1706\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1707\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1708\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1709\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1710\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1711\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1712\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1713\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1714\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1715\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1716\t`:blake3`.\n  1717\t\n  1718\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1719\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1720\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1721\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1722\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1723\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1724\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1725\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1726\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1727\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1728\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1729\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1730\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1731\t\n  1732\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1733\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (a signed assertion\n  1734\tby a declared principal resolves; a bare `:asserted-by` with no proof is\n  1735\t`:unauthenticated`; a bad signature is `:unauthenticated`; an attested\n  1736\tlog's assertion copied onto another stream is `:unauthenticated`; an\n  1737\tundeclared principal is ignored; a signed retraction bound to an\n  1738\tassertion's id removes that assertion only, and a retraction naming no\n  1739\tassertion or signed by another principal is discarded; an exact\n  1740\tduplicate envelope is honored once and never counted as equivocation;\n  1741\ta replayed sequence and a distinct equivocating pair are discarded; two\n  1742\tproven assertions refuse `:ambiguous-name`; snapshot advance). Then:\n  1743\tthe manifest and derivation\n  1744\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1745\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1746\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1747\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1748\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1749\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1750\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1751\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1752\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1753\twhere the `:yin.ast/code` tree is not the manifest's tree); a\n  1754\tsame-named primitive of different profile at the receiver is\n  1755\t`:unresolved-free`; a shadowed export name in the requiring program's\n  1756\tstore is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n  1757\t`:undeclared-free`; two outstanding requires on one response stream\n  1758\teach restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n  1759\thave been polled is not skipped; a module requiring another links\n  1760\ttransitively while a third task keeps running; a require cycle is\n  1761\t`:require-cycle`; a module that binds a name and exports a closure\n  1762\treading it links, the closure reads the module's value in the\n  1763\tparent, a parent binding of the same name neither supplies nor\n  1764\tshadows it, and a write from one export is visible to the next\n  1765\tapplication in the same task and to no other task; a read inside a\n  1766\tbody applied before its definition retains its obligation and is\n  1767\t`:undeclared-free` unless the manifest declares it; an export-only\n  1768\timage with no application site produces no obligations; a parked\n  1769\tentry recorded before an attach restores after it at the same pcs\n  1770\twith `:segment` never assigned from the entry; two tasks holding\n  1771\timages of different lengths require the same module and each applies\n  1772\tits export correctly; `(vm :stack)` and `(vm :register)` in `yin.repl` link\n  1773\tthe same manifest by H and R respectively and produce B0-equal results.\n  1774\t\n  1775\t**M5. `yin.repl` wiring.** The REPL composes the link pair per VM and\n  1776\tthe content pair per connection (`connect` already opens the RPC\n  1777\tclient). `(require 'foo)` at the prompt exercises the whole path.\n  1778\t\n  1779\tCoexistence during M4: host modules are entered by\n  1780\t`register-host-module` from the first commit of M4, so every existing\n  1781\tcomposition keeps working while linked modules are added. There is no\n  1782\tperiod in which two registry shapes coexist.\n  1783\t\n  1784\t## 10. File box\n  1785\t\n  1786\t```text\n  1787\tRenamed:  src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc\n  1788\t            -> src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc            (M1)\n  1789\t          test/yin/vm/debruijn_linker_test.cljc\n  1790\t            -> test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc           (M1)\n  1791\tNew:      test/yin/vm/linker_step_test.cljc           (M3)\n  1792\t          test/yin/vm/linker_authority_test.cljc      (M4 entry)\n  1793\t          test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc        (M4)\n  1794\tEdited:   src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc                 (M4)\n  1795\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc  (:link-request, :link-response,\n  1796\t                                        :install wait reasons; the\n  1797\t                                        install child; module-store\n  1798\t                                        resolution)                 (M4)\n  1799\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/content.cljc (retire load-rows,\n  1800\t                                        fetch-vector)              (M2)\n  1801\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc, semantic.cljc,\n  1802\t          debruijn/stack.cljc, debruijn/register.cljc\n  1803\t            (attach-image; offset table and image\n  1804\t             identities on the positional kernels; row index\n  1805\t             on the walker; closures carry :store-of)              (M4)\n  1806\t          src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc  (append-*-image over attach-image;\n  1807\t                                   the four streams)          (M4, M5)\n  1808\t          docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n  1809\t            (section 7.4.1 rows, 7.4.3 variants, 7.5.1 marker\n  1810\t             keys :yin.k/binding and :yin.k/store-of)              (M4)\n  1811\tDepends:  dao.jing (segment-key, segment-matches?, materialize!)\n  1812\t          dao.jing.remote, dao.jing.remote.step, dao.stream.rpc\n  1813\t          yin.vm (validate-rows, free-names, primitive-profiles)\n  1814\t          yin.vm.code (well-formed-vector?)\n  1815\t          yin.vm.ledger (derive-record, verify-derivation)\n  1816\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n  1817\tMust not change:\n  1818\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n  1819\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing. No kernel's step function\n  1820\t          changes its decode, dispatch, or register model; the one\n  1821\t          behavioral amendment r6 makes at a kernel is closure-\n  1822\t          directed free resolution (7.3), the :store-of consult.\n  1823\t```\n  1824\t\n  1825\t`yin.vm.linker` exports: `fetch`, `verify`, `discharge`, `link-state`,\n  1826\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon`, `publish!`, `ast-format`,\n  1827\t`semantic-format`, `stack-format`, `register-format`, `manifest-format`,\n  1828\t`record-format`, the four free-name, definition, and application-site\n  1829\tscanners, `row-local-defect`, `index-from-datoms`, `address-attribute`,\n  1830\t`trusted-fallback`, `verifying-fallback`, `refused`, `refused?`, `ok?`,\n  1831\t`refusal-reasons`.\n  1832\t\n  1990\t\n  1991\t## 13. Reconciliation record\n  1992\t\n  1993\t### 13.1 Revision r6 (round 5, `gpt-6-sol`)\n  1994\t\n  1995\tThe round-5 review closed the wait-entry id and duplicate-authority\n  1996\titems (no action) and left two partial findings plus one new defect.\n  1997\tEach, and what r6 did:\n  1998\t\n  1999\t| Item                              | Resolution                        |\n  2000\t|-----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n  2001\t| A lambda read was discharged by   | Agreed. A body occurrence is now  |\n  2002\t| any later unconditional           | discharged only by a definition   |\n  2003\t| definition, an early application  | proven to precede every           |\n  2004\t| was left to fail at run time,     | application site, every site      |\n  2005\t| and the record examples returned  | being a possible application of   |\n  2006\t| name sets                         | every closure; export-only        |\n  2007\t|                                   | images discharge against all      |\n  2008\t|                                   | unconditional definitions, whose  |\n  2009\t|                                   | post-halt reads run against the   |\n  2010\t|                                   | module store; the run-time        |\n  2011\t|                                   | error claim is withdrawn --       |\n  2012\t|                                   | `resolve-var` falls through to    |\n  2013\t|                                   | ambient bindings; `:applications- |\n  2014\t|                                   | fn` joins the record and all      |\n  2015\t|                                   | four examples return the section  |\n  2016\t|                                   | 4.1 records (4.1, 4.2 step 5a,   |\n  2017\t|                                   | 5.1-5.4).                         |\n  2018\t| `attach-image` changed `:hash`,   | Agreed. Entries record a per-image|\n  2019\t| so parked entries were refused    | identity checked against the      |\n  2020\t| or rewound the code space, and    | offset table, never the           |\n  2021\t| one parent's lowered bindings     | concatenation `:hash`; restores   |\n  2022\t| were published to every waiter    | write registers and never         |\n  2023\t|                                   | `:segment`; lifted continuations  |\n  2024\t|                                   | carry image-relative pcs rebased  |\n  2025\t|                                   | on lower; the scheduler registry  |\n  2026\t|                                   | holds the portable slice and each |\n  2027\t|                                   | receiving task attaches and       |\n  2028\t|                                   | lowers against its own            |\n  2029\t|                                   | coordinates (7.3 acts 3-4, 8.3). |\n  2030\t| New P1: a module-local store      | Agreed. The child's halted store  |\n  2031\t| binding was lost on export; the   | lifts as `:yin.k/store` beside    |\n  2032\t| closure read the parent's store   | the exports; closure markers name |\n  2033\t|                                   | `:yin.k/store-of` the manifest    |\n  2034\t|                                   | address; each receiving task      |\n  2035\t|                                   | lowers an isolated `:module-      |\n  2036\t|                                   | stores` entry; closure-body free  |\n  2037\t|                                   | reads and writes resolve through  |\n  2038\t|                                   | it, never the ambient store --    |\n  2039\t|                                   | UCF 7.6.2's no-merge rule at      |\n  2040\t|                                   | module grain (7.3, 8.3).          |\n  2041\t\n  2042\t### 13.2 Revision r5 (round 4, `gpt-6-sol`)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
