{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1833,1945p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1833\t## 11. Completion criteria\n  1834\t\n  1835\tStructure:\n  1836\t\n  1837\t1. One `fetch` and one `step` serve all four formats with no\n  1838\t   format-specific branching; a fifth format is one record.\n  1839\t2. No global loader, registry, callback, or cache; every input is an\n  1840\t   argument or VM-state value; no function or handle ever appears in a\n  1841\t   value on the link or content streams.\n  1842\t3. Tri-host parity (JVM, Node, ClojureDart), 0 kondo errors, clean\n  1843\t   cljstyle.\n  1844\t4. This file and `yin.vm.linker` are pure ASCII with every line at most\n  1845\t   80 columns.\n  1846\t\n  1847\tVerification:\n  1848\t\n  1849\t5. Every B6 completion criterion (section 11 there) holds for all four\n  1850\t   formats where applicable, through both `fetch` and `step`.\n  1851\t6. A payload whose address is valid but whose identity is not the one\n  1852\t   requested is refused for every format, including the two whose\n  1853\t   identity is a storage address, and under every registered algorithm.\n  1854\t7. A request naming a contract the format record does not implement is\n  1855\t   `:contract-mismatch` before validation runs.\n  1856\t8. A malformed row is refused before any of its children is requested,\n  1857\t   and every composition bound produces `:parts-limit`.\n  1858\t9. Local `fetch` produces exactly the content-pair traffic the stepped\n  1859\t   path produces and holds no content handle.\n  1860\t\n  1861\tRequire:\n  1862\t\n  1863\t10. `(require 'foo)` on each of the four backends, over ring buffers,\n  1864\t    parks, links, installs through the child phases, and resumes with\n  1865\t    `'foo`; the same over the JVM WebSocket content path.\n  1866\t11. The scheduler registry holds no function that arrived by linking\n  1867\t    and no lowered bindings, only the portable slice; every task-local\n  1868\t    `:bindings` was lowered from a slice an isolated child evaluation\n  1869\t    produced, which reached halt with every export bound.\n  1870\t12. UCF section 7.4.1 carries `:link-request`, `:link-response`, and\n  1871\t    `:install` safepoints, section 7.4.3 their pending variants, section\n  1872\t    7.5.1 the `:yin.k/binding` closure variants and `:yin.k/store-of`\n  1873\t    key of section 7.3, and a parked entry of each kind lifts and\n  1874\t    lowers through UCF's round-trip test.\n  1875\t13. Every swapped-image and swapped-name case in M4 refuses before load.\n  1876\t14. The assertion policy of section 8.2 refuses `:ambiguous-name`,\n  1877\t    discards unproven assertions as `:unauthenticated`, and ignores\n  1878\t    undeclared principals, at a fixed snapshot.\n  1879\t15. A module that defines a name and then reads it in the main\n  1880\t    sequence produces no obligation for that name; a main-sequence\n  1881\t    read before the definition is `:use-before-definition`; a read\n  1882\t    inside a body is free of obligation only when an unconditional\n  1883\t    definition dominates every application site, and retains it\n  1884\t    otherwise -- an application preceding the definition, a closure\n  1885\t    handed to an import, a scanner with no application positions --\n  1886\t    linking then only if the manifest declares it; an export-only\n  1887\t    image with no application site discharges body reads against its\n  1888\t    unconditional definitions; a name defined only inside an `:if`\n  1889\t    branch and read afterwards retains its obligation; a scanner\n  1890\t    with no positions retains every obligation; an export whose key\n  1891\t    is computed at run time is neither refused statically nor\n  1892\t    assumed, and is verified at `validated`.\n  1893\t16. Two install children and the root task, each with counter `0`,\n  1894\t    issue three requests on one link pair with three distinct ids, and\n  1895\t    each restores on its own.\n  1896\t17. On every backend, an exported closure applied in the parent after\n  1897\t    `linked` runs the same body it ran in the child; a stack and a\n  1898\t    register closure exported from a child whose image was appended at\n  1899\t    a nonzero offset in the parent resolve to the relocated pc; a\n  1900\t    walker closure lowers to a body structurally equal to the child's;\n  1901\t    on every backend, a parent parked mid-program at a nonzero pc with\n  1902\t    a non-empty stack, frames, and continuation resumes after\n  1903\t    `attach-image` at the same pc with the same stack, frames, and\n  1904\t    restore identities, and every register the loader would have reset\n  1905\t    is unchanged; the parked entry predates the attach, its recorded\n  1906\t    image is a row of the offset table, no restore writes `:segment`\n  1907\t    from an entry, and `:hash` is never a restore key; a continuation\n  1908\t    lifted after an attach and lowered into a fresh kernel places\n  1909\t    every pc by the receiving offset table; two waiters holding\n  1910\t    images of different lengths each lower the same slice against\n  1911\t    their own coordinates and apply the export correctly.\n  1912\t18. Under `:derivation :verifying`, a manifest whose record names a\n  1913\t    profile the linker does not implement is `:unverified-derivation`,\n  1914\t    never installed; under `:trusted` the same manifest installs with\n  1915\t    `:trust :composition` in the outcome.\n  1916\t19. A request naming a mismatched contract is refused with no content\n  1917\t    request appended and no validator run.\n  1918\t20. A closure re-exported from a transitive dependency lifts with that\n  1919\t    dependency's image as origin, the parent loads that image before\n  1920\t    lowering, and an origin the scheduler never verified is\n  1921\t    `:foreign-image`; a positional marker offered to a named kernel is\n  1922\t    `:binding-mismatch`.\n  1923\t21. An exact duplicate of a valid envelope, appended any number of\n  1924\t    times, is honored exactly once and never marks its principal as\n  1925\t    equivocating; a replayed envelope with an old sequence, an envelope\n  1926\t    at or below a principal's floor, two distinct envelopes with one\n  1927\t    sequence, a retraction naming no assertion, and a retraction by\n  1928\t    another principal are each discarded with the stated kind; a\n  1929\t    retraction bound to an assertion's id removes that assertion only.\n  1930\t22. One four-way manifest links through all four kernels with no\n  1931\t    `:contract-mismatch`; a manifest of another schema version is\n  1932\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`; a derivation without a\n  1933\t    contract entry is `:descriptor-defect` with rule\n  1934\t    `:contract-missing`.\n  1935\t23. On every backend, a module that binds `(def x 1)` and exports a\n  1936\t    closure reading `x` links, and the closure applied in the parent\n  1937\t    reads the module's `x`, while a parent binding of the same name\n  1938\t    neither supplies nor shadows it; a write the closure makes to `x`\n  1939\t    is visible to a sibling export applied afterwards in the same\n  1940\t    task and to no other task's module store; the same module linked\n  1941\t    by two tasks holds two isolated stores; in the child, a closure\n  1942\t    re-exported from a dependency reads that dependency's module\n  1943\t    store, not the child's ambient bindings.\n  1944\t\n  1945\t## 12. Open decisions\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
